<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kothi State</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1950 CE (approx.) · capital Kothi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Baghel Rajput principality of Baghelkhand said by family tradition to have branched off from the Sohawal ruling family.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kothi was held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghel">Baghel Rajputs</a> and, according to family tradition, emerged as a separate holding from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sohawal-state">Sohawal State</a>, itself a cadet branch of the Baghel house of Rewa. The register dates it from 1600, but the details of its separation are known mainly from family tradition.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Raja ruled a few dozen villages in the upland country west of Rewa. In the British period Kothi was a non-salute state under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghelkhand-agency">Baghelkhand Agency</a> of Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and little else of its internal history is widely recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kothi was merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vindhya-pradesh">Vindhya Pradesh</a> in 1948, which became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956. Its lands lie in today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satna-district">Satna district</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kothi-state.jpg" alt="Kothi State" width="320" height="199"><figcaption>Image: Great Britain India Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kothi-Bhaisunda_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kothi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bagheli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kothi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1775&amp;focus=kothi-state" aria-label="Kothi State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6824 1266 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kothi State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7144 1522L7364 1601M7144 1522L7364 1602M7144 1522L7160 1530"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7160 1530h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7144 1522h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7144 1522h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1775&amp;focus=kothi-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
